{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>He is Aharon and Moshe.</b> Meaning, those traced in the genealogy of the passage — they are the ones <b>concerning whom HaShem said to them, 'Bring them out.'</b> Meaning, because they possess the power to bring them out, for they are kings over Pharaoh king of Egypt and over the children of Israel, as he explained in the verse ״וַיְצַוֵּם״. Therefore <b>HaShem said to them, 'Bring out the children of Israel from the land of Egypt'</b>, and whoever refuses — they shall strike him with the rod of discipline that HaShem has prepared for the guts of fools."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:11.577909290Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}